# Text files: detected automatically, stored and checked out with LF endings.
# "text=auto" rather than a bare "text" matters. Setting it outright declares
# every file in the repository to be text, which overrides Git's own detection
# and strips CR bytes out of binaries as they are committed. Nothing complains:
# the file is compared after that same normalisation, so it reads as unchanged
# while what is stored no longer matches what is on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, kept byte for byte. Auto-detection already covers these; naming them
# is the belt to its braces, since the failure is silent and only shows up in a
# fresh clone.
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.psd binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
